  "notes": "Two Units share MCRAC/MCREC systems; treated as one LER anchored to Unit 2 per docket 05000321 (Unit 1 docket would be 05000366, not provided in FORM-366 fields). Alpha MCRAC low-refrigerant failure is a genuinely separate, concurrent failure mode not caused by the personnel-error cause code, but both converge on the shared consequence of multiple TS-prohibited conditions due to overlapping MCRAC/MCREC inoperabilities. No BACKED_UP_BY edges asserted because Charlie MCRAC was itself intermittently inoperable due to tagouts, and Alpha/Charlie operability during the event was not uniformly stated as continuously available. No previous similar events per narrative. PART_OF not asserted for CDU->MCRAC per explicit-only rule (narrative describes it as 'condensing unit of the MCRAC subsystem' which arguably supports containment, but kept conservative given ambiguity of exact phrasing); could be revisited if stricter PART_OF desired."
